  "Question": "A school library's collection increases from 5 ten-thousand volumes to 7.2 ten-thousand volumes over two years. Let the average annual growth rate be \\(x\\). Which equation can be set up?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5(1+x)^2=7.2\\)",
    "B": "\\(5(1+2x)=7.2\\)",
    "C": "\\(5+x^2=7.2\\)",
    "D": "\\(5(1+x)=7.2\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "With the same growth rate each year, the collection after two years is \\(5(1+x)^2\\), so the equation is \\(5(1+x)^2=7.2\\). B treats compound growth as simple growth.",
